WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How is your --
is your dog, Petunia,

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:04.137
enjoying the quality time
she's getting with you?

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think she is.
She's snoring.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:08.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if this audio
can pick it up.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's laying on a little towel
She's enjoying it.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:15.115
I think it took her a couple -
It took her more than a week

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.383 line:92%
to realize what was happening,

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is that
we weren't going anywhere.

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:22.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've taken her out
on the street a couple times

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.391 size:84% position:42% line:92%
safely, with a mask on.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
Totally kidding.
-Right.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Her face is flat.
It would suffocate her.

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:34.100
-And she just looks around
like, empty streets, like...

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.735 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Like, no one anywhere.

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:38.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's really weird to a dog
-Yeah. Our dog is --

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Her whole life,
she's at leg level.

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now there's none.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.045
There's no legs
to mark exactly how tall she is.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's no legs.
She doesn't know -- yeah.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.449
She can't tell a quarter
from the Statue of Liberty

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's got no --
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:53.987 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
--Without legs.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You went back.

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
You hosted "SNL"
for a third time.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.159 line:92%
-Yeah, and then the world ended.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.126 line:92%
-Yeah, and the world ended

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in February, right?
February.

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was leap year, Saturday,
February 29th.

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:10.804
-And you -- you had to cance
a stand-up show in Canada?

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:14.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I --
Yeah, but I'm --

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:17.243 line:92%
I'm gonna get there real soon.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, Toronto, yes?

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Toronto, Canada.
-Yeah.

00:01:21.114 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Supposed to perform
in the fall.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:23.883 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Had an emergency.

00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
Truly had an emergency,
couldn't perform.

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:27.353 line:92%
By the way, no one cares.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're still mad at me
for canceling the first time

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can tell them my legs
were chopped off,

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they'd be like,
"Well, you should've let

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.329 size:75% position:38% line:92%
ticket owners know."

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then weather-related
cancellation.

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:42.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I rescheduled
for February 28th.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.904
And I say, "There's no way
this is gonna be cancelled."

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:47.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then I cancelled it
for "Saturday Night Live."

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.780
Now it's going to be rescheduled
for the fourth time real soon.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had Lorne
write a letter for you.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.119 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, Lorne is the --

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he has
a dukedom in Canada.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Or a fiefdom or something

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he's a Knight of the Orde
of Canada.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'd tell you that,
and so --

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wait. He wears --
He's got the little button

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They have a little button
yeah.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A lapel pin.
I should make clear, it's not,

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.470 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think, a button.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not a -- No.
It doesn't have a pin

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the back, and it says,
"I'm in Canada."

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's small,
understated lapel pin.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:24.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Looks very nice.

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:27.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he wrote a letter
to his own people

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
to ask for their forgiveness
for me missing the date.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And it was very nice.

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I am really excited
to see the people of Toronto

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do --
This isn't like a life bit

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I keep can canceling
the show for fun.

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not a sociopath
in that way.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
I recognize
how that would be funny.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:46.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I am not
currently doing that.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-Well, all the good people

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.172 line:92%
of Canada and every great nation

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:55.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
has a chance to hear you
and Nick Kroll.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:57.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'll be right back to tal
to talk about the

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.578 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Oh, Hello: the P'dcast"

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
right after this.
-Thank you.

